  "status_text": "Two more statements for every size were checked in Lean within the hour they were filed, from outside contributors: to represent the double crown on 2k + 2k vertices takes at least 5k - 3 AND/OR gates of fan-in at most two, for every k of at least 2; to represent the complement of an N-by-N matching takes at least 2N AND, OR and NOT gates of fan-in at most two, every gate counted, from N = 3. Still a conjecture on the desk: the cycle bound; on paper it is one lemma away, and that lemma survived a search over every circuit of at most 6 gates (computed, not checked).",
